            <ArticleTitle>ACOG Committee Opinion No. 376: Nalbuphine hydrochloride use for intrapartum analgesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>449</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Safety concerns have been raised regarding the use of nalbuphine hydrochloride during labor. The American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists finds data are insufficient to recommend any changes in nalbuphine hydrochloride administration at this time.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
